      "result": "It keeps them. The leftover items come back as a final, shorter list. Nothing is padded and nothing is dropped:\n\n```python\n>>> from more_itertools import chunked\n>>> list(chunked([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8], 3))\n[[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6], [7, 8]]\n```\n\nYou can change this in two ways:\n\n- **`strict=True`**: `chunked(iterable, n, strict=True)` raises a `ValueError` if the last chunk would be shorter than `n`.\n- **Padding**: if you want the last chunk filled out to size `n`, use `more_itertools.grouper(iterable, n, incomplete='fill', fillvalue=...)`. Note that `grouper` returns tuples, not lists.",
